Implementation of atoi() and ftoi() in C

📌 Project Description

This project implements the functionality of the standard C library functions "atoi()" and "ftoi()" using user-defined functions.

The main objective of this project is to understand how numeric values can be converted from one data type to another without directly using the standard conversion functions.

🔹 atoi()

"atoi()" stands for ASCII to Integer. It converts a numeric string into an integer value.

For example:

Input  : "12345"
Output : 12345

The implementation handles:

- Positive numbers
- Negative numbers
- Optional "+" or "-" sign
- Conversion of numeric characters into integer values

🔹 ftoi()

"ftoi()" converts a floating-point number into an integer.

For example:

Input  : 123.45
Output : 123

The fractional part is removed during the conversion.

🎯 Objectives

- Understand string-to-integer conversion.
- Understand floating-point-to-integer conversion.
- Implement conversion logic using C programming.
- Practice loops, conditions, operators, and functions.
- Understand how library functions work internally.

🛠️ Technologies Used

- Programming Language: C
- Compiler: GCC / Any standard C compiler
- Concepts: Functions, loops, conditional statements, strings, arithmetic operators, type conversion

